{
  "name": "fork_1_phase3_room_pin_steers_the_night_like_the_sleep_sensor",
  "description": "Fork Dunky13#1 phase 3 (docs/preference-learning-spec.md). The Issue #1194 closed-loop cold night replayed with no sleep sensor configured: instead, preference learning is on, the bedroom sensor is a selected room and the night is pinned to it. The room context drives the same remote-offset loop, so every setpoint write between bedtime and wake is identical to the sleep-sensor night, and the wake write is the plain 68 F.",
  "source": "docs/preference-learning-spec.md, Phase 3, Steering reference per part of day: a pinned room steers exactly like the sleep-window bedroom sensor (same loop, step, cap, startup wait and fall-back).",
  "issue": "Dunky13#1",
  "notes": [
    "Occupant impact: a household that picks the bedroom for the night (rather than configuring the sleep sensor) gets the same warm bedroom, by the same thermostat nudges.",
    "Derived from remote_offset_1194e_closed_loop_night_cold_bedroom_swing_1_5: identical events and expected writes; only the reference configuration differs.",
    "(a) Effectiveness: with the room context ignored, the loop never arms and the writes collapse to the plain 66/68 F targets, so the setpoint_writes assertion fails.",
    "(c) Occupant outcome if this fails to catch a regression: a pinned bedroom silently stops steering, and the bedroom stays cold at night."
  ],
